{"timestamp":"2026-05-12T02:22:24.121Z","type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"mcp_tool_call_end","call_id":"call_BZRiC5ts4X6pv6TwmncsQepe","invocation":{"server":"codex_apps","tool":"github_get_pr_info","arguments":{"repository_full_name":"entireio/cli","pr_number":1184}},"duration":{"secs":1,"nanos":389337250},"result":{"Ok":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1184\", \"number\": 1184, \"state\": \"open\", \"merged\": false, \"mergeable\": true, \"draft\": false, \"body\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/359\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n## Summary\\n\\nFixes bug #3 from the broader review observability sweep: the Ctrl+O drill-in view was unhelpful because each event was truncated to one terminal-wide line, navigation was limited to \\u2191/\\u2193, and the whole view became unavailable after both agents finished (any key dismissed the TUI). This PR replaces the manual scroll math with `bubbles/v2/viewport`, wraps long events to multiple lines, adds standard pager keys + mouse wheel, keeps Ctrl+O usable post-finish, and adds visible cancellation feedback so users see \\\"agents are stopping\\\" instead of staring at a still-spinning dashboard.\\n\\n## What lands\\n\\n**Five commits, each independently sensible:**\\n\\n1. **`a9210fb9f` \\u2014 Viewport widget + multi-line wrap + key delegation**\\n   - Replaces `detailScroll int` field with `bubbles/v2/viewport` widget. Viewport owns scroll state, key bindings, and rendering.\\n   - New `wrapDisplayWidth(s, width) []string` helper in `tui_text.go` mirroring `truncateDisplayWidth`. Preserves embedded newlines as paragraph boundaries (load-bearing for multi-paragraph AssistantText).\\n   - `eventLine` \\u2192 `eventLines` returning `[]string`. Each event renders as one or more wrapped lines instead of one truncated line.\\n   - `detailView` \\u2192 `detailFrame` (header + viewport body + footer, padded to `termHeight`).\\n   - Unhandled keys in detail mode forward to `viewport.Update` \\u2014 PgUp/PgDn/Home/End/g/G/u/d/j/k all work via viewport's internal keymap.\\n   - Removed `~130 lines` of manual windowing logic (`buildBodyLines`, `maxDetailScroll`, `clampScroll`).\\n\\n2. **`27fd1baca` \\u2014 Post-finish access + visible cancellation feedback**\\n   - Replaces \\\"any key quits when finished\\\" with explicit quit keys only: `q` / `Esc` / `Enter` / `Ctrl+C`. Other keys including `Ctrl+O` fall through, so users can drill into completed agent buffers for post-mortem inspection.\\n   - Updated post-finish footer: `Ctrl+O: drill in \\u00b7 q/Esc/Enter: exit` (replaces the misleading \\\"Press any key to exit.\\\")\\n   - New `cancelling bool` flag on `reviewTUIModel`. First Ctrl+C sets it and fires the shared CancelFunc once via `cancelOnce`. Second Ctrl+C during drain emits `tea.Quit` immediately for force-quit.\\n   - When `cancelling`, dashboard rows for still-running agents show `cancelling` status text (10 chars, fits the existing column).\\n   - Footer during cancellation: `Cancelling agents... \\u00b7 Ctrl+C again: force quit`.\\n\\n3. **`998ddfd1e` \\u2014 Enable mouse mode in detail-mode View**\\n   - In bubbletea v2, mouse mode is a per-View field (`v.MouseMode = tea.MouseModeCellMotion`), not a Program option. Only enabled while in detail mode so dashboard preserves normal terminal mouse-select for copy/paste.\\n\\n4. **`6fb988b43` \\u2014 Doc comment fixup**\\n   - `tui_sink.go` doc on `RunFinished` still described the pre-Commit-2 \\\"press any key to dismiss\\\" behavior. Updated to reflect explicit-exit-keys + Ctrl+O drill-in availability. Comment-only change.\\n\\n5. **`c279308b2` \\u2014 Route mouse events to viewport** (the actual wheel-scroll wire-up)\\n   - Setting `View.MouseMode` made the bubbletea Program receive mouse events from the terminal, but the `Update` switch only routed `tea.KeyPressMsg` to `handleKey` and `tea.WindowSizeMsg` to the resize handler. Mouse events fell through to the catch-all `return m, nil` and never reached the viewport.\\n   - Added a switch case forwarding `tea.MouseWheelMsg`, `tea.MouseClickMsg`, `tea.MouseReleaseMsg`, `tea.MouseMotionMsg` to `m.detail.Update` when in detail mode. Viewport's `MouseWheelEnabled` is true by default so wheel scroll just works.\\n   - Includes `TestTUIModel_DelegatesMouseWheelToViewport` regression test.\\n\\n## Smoke evidence\\n\\nEnd-to-end verified on this branch with a real `entire review` run:\\n- \\u2705 Mouse wheel scrolls through buffered events\\n- \\u2705 Long AssistantText events wrap to multiple readable lines (no `\\u2026` truncation mid-content)\\n- Drill-in chrome and key delegation confirmed via unit tests (`TestDetailFrame_*`, `TestTUIModel_DelegatesScrollKeysToViewport`, `TestTUIModel_DelegatesMouseWheelToViewport`)\\n\\n## What this PR does NOT do (explicitly deferred)\\n\\n- **Agent-failure visibility** (the \\\"dashboard shows \\u2713 done but tally says 1 failed\\\" inconsistency): fixed by [#1167](https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1167) which is already open with reviews approved. Once #1167 lands, the synthetic RunError emission from `proc.Wait()` errors will surface in the drill-in event log AND the runFinishedMsg handler will propagate Failed status correctly. Independent of this PR.\\n- **Env-handshake / session-tagging bug** (the \\\"review session was not tagged as a review\\\" warning when synthesis is declined): separate follow-up. The PR fix here doesn't claim to address that path.\\n- **Per-agent progress streaming**: agents like claude-code `-p` and codex `exec` buffer their stdout until the response is complete, so during the run the drill-in shows mostly `[started]` until the buffer flushes at the end. Improving live streaming requires per-agent investigation (different output modes for each agent CLI) \\u2014 that's its own brainstorm.\\n- **Bubbletea v1 \\u2192 v2 mouse API**: I originally planned `tea.WithMouseCellMotion()` as a Program option (v1 idiom); v2 moved this to `View.MouseMode`. Adapted accordingly with regression test.\\n\\n## Test plan\\n\\n- [x] `mise run fmt && mise run lint` \\u2014 0 issues\\n- [x] `go test ./cmd/entire/cli/review/ -count=1` \\u2014 all green (includes 3 new tests for wrap, viewport init, scroll-key delegation, mouse-wheel delegation, post-finish access, cancellation feedback)\\n- [x] Manual smoke: mouse wheel scrolls during real multi-agent review\\n- [x] Unit-tested all key delegation paths (keyboard + mouse)\\n\\n## Two-stage subagent review per task\\n\\nBoth Commits 1 and 2 went through spec-compliance + code-quality review:\\n- **Commit 1 (viewport)**: spec \\u2705, code quality \\u2705\\n- **Commit 2 (post-finish + cancellation)**: spec \\u2705, code quality \\u2705 (after `6fb988b43` doc fixup)\\n- **Commit 3 (mouse mode)**: DONE_WITH_CONCERNS \\u2014 accepted v2 API adaptation, then the missing routing was found and fixed in `c279308b2` with regression test\\n\\n\\ud83e\\udd16 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\\n\\n<!-- CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\\n---\\n\\n> [!NOTE]\\n> **Medium Risk**\\n> Moderate risk: replaces manual drill-in scrolling with a `viewport.Model` and changes key/mouse handling and cancellation/exit semantics, which can affect interactive TUI behavior but is well-covered by new tests.\\n> \\n> **Overview**\\n> Improves the Ctrl+O drill-in by switching its body rendering to a `bubbles/v2/viewport`, so long `AssistantText` now **wraps to multiple lines**, preserves embedded newlines as paragraph breaks, and supports standard pager keys plus mouse-wheel scrolling.\\n> \\n> Refactors the drill-in renderer into `detailFrame` (chrome + padding) and removes the prior manual scroll/windowing logic, adding helpers like `wrapDisplayWidth` and viewport-driven auto-tail that preserves user scroll when not at bottom.\\n> \\n> Updates run-finish and cancellation UX: post-finish no longer exits on any key (explicit `q/Esc/Enter/Ctrl+C` only, while `Ctrl+O` still works), and Ctrl+C now enters a visible *cancelling* state on first press with a second Ctrl+C force-quitting. Tests are updated/expanded to cover wrapping, viewport delegation, mouse routing, and the new exit/cancel behavior.\\n> \\n> <sup>Reviewed by [Cursor Bugbot](https://cursor.com/bugbot) for commit c279308b22d7bc77a43ad2f580523023d302b3c1. Configure [here](https://www.cursor.com/dashboard/bugbot).</sup>\\n<!-- /CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\", \"title\": \"feat(review): viewport-driven drill-in with wrap, scroll, and post-finish access\", \"base\": \"main\", \"base_sha\": \"40d00ad55459990a0cd6412b19d859c02498266c\", \"head\": \"feat/review-detail-viewport\", \"head_sha\": \"c279308b22d7bc77a43ad2f580523023d302b3c1\", \"merge_commit_sha\": \"83ec38611832c7bcb1ada2d694cf51514384c7d6\", \"user\": {\"login\": \"peyton-alt\", \"name\": \"peyton-alt\", \"email\": null, \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/249787869?v=4\", \"id\": 249787869}, \"requested_reviewers\": null, \"requested_team_reviewers\": [{\"slug\": \"cli-maintainers\", \"name\": \"cli-maintainers\"}], \"diff\": null, \"comments\": null, \"created_at\": \"2026-05-12T01:58:57Z\", \"updated_at\": \"2026-05-12T02:13:32Z\", \"closed_at\": null, \"merged_at\": null, \"commits\": 5, \"changed_files\": 7, \"additions\": 695, \"deletions\": 294, \"display_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1184\", \"display_title\": \"feat(review): viewport-driven drill-in with wrap, scroll, and post-finish access\"}"}],"structuredContent":{"url":"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1184","number":1184,"state":"open","merged":false,"mergeable":true,"draft":false,"body":"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/359\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\n\n## Summary\n\nFixes bug #3 from the broader review observability sweep: the Ctrl+O drill-in view was unhelpful because each event was truncated to one terminal-wide line, navigation was limited to ↑/↓, and the whole view became unavailable after both agents finished (any key dismissed the TUI). This PR replaces the manual scroll math with `bubbles/v2/viewport`, wraps long events to multiple lines, adds standard pager keys + mouse wheel, keeps Ctrl+O usable post-finish, and adds visible cancellation feedback so users see \"agents are stopping\" instead of staring at a still-spinning dashboard.\n\n## What lands\n\n**Five commits, each independently sensible:**\n\n1. **`a9210fb9f` — Viewport widget + multi-line wrap + key delegation**\n   - Replaces `detailScroll int` field with `bubbles/v2/viewport` widget. Viewport owns scroll state, key bindings, and rendering.\n   - New `wrapDisplayWidth(s, width) []string` helper in `tui_text.go` mirroring `truncateDisplayWidth`. Preserves embedded newlines as paragraph boundaries (load-bearing for multi-paragraph AssistantText).\n   - `eventLine` → `eventLines` returning `[]string`. Each event renders as one or more wrapped lines instead of one truncated line.\n   - `detailView` → `detailFrame` (header + viewport body + footer, padded to `termHeight`).\n   - Unhandled keys in detail mode forward to `viewport.Update` — PgUp/PgDn/Home/End/g/G/u/d/j/k all work via viewport's internal keymap.\n   - Removed `~130 lines` of manual windowing logic (`buildBodyLines`, `maxDetailScroll`, `clampScroll`).\n\n2. **`27fd1baca` — Post-finish access + visible cancellation feedback**\n   - Replaces \"any key quits when finished\" with explicit quit keys only: `q` / `Esc` / `Enter` / `Ctrl+C`. Other keys including `Ctrl+O` fall through, so users can drill into completed agent buffers for post-mortem inspection.\n   - Updated post-finish footer: `Ctrl+O: drill in · q/Esc/Enter: exit` (replaces the misleading \"Press any key to exit.\")\n   - New `cancelling bool` flag on `reviewTUIModel`. First Ctrl+C sets it and fires the shared CancelFunc once via `cancelOnce`. Second Ctrl+C during drain emits `tea.Quit` immediately for force-quit.\n   - When `cancelling`, dashboard rows for still-running agents show `cancelling` status text (10 chars, fits the existing column).\n   - Footer during cancellation: `Cancelling agents... · Ctrl+C again: force quit`.\n\n3. **`998ddfd1e` — Enable mouse mode in detail-mode View**\n   - In bubbletea v2, mouse mode is a per-View field (`v.MouseMode = tea.MouseModeCellMotion`), not a Program option. Only enabled while in detail mode so dashboard preserves normal terminal mouse-select for copy/paste.\n\n4. **`6fb988b43` — Doc comment fixup**\n   - `tui_sink.go` doc on `RunFinished` still described the pre-Commit-2 \"press any key to dismiss\" behavior. Updated to reflect explicit-exit-keys + Ctrl+O drill-in availability. Comment-only change.\n\n5. **`c279308b2` — Route mouse events to viewport** (the actual wheel-scroll wire-up)\n   - Setting `View.MouseMode` made the bubbletea Program receive mouse events from the terminal, but the `Update` switch only routed `tea.KeyPressMsg` to `handleKey` and `tea.WindowSizeMsg` to the resize handler. Mouse events fell through to the catch-all `return m, nil` and never reached the viewport.\n   - Added a switch case forwarding `tea.MouseWheelMsg`, `tea.MouseClickMsg`, `tea.MouseReleaseMsg`, `tea.MouseMotionMsg` to `m.detail.Update` when in detail mode. Viewport's `MouseWheelEnabled` is true by default so wheel scroll just works.\n   - Includes `TestTUIModel_DelegatesMouseWheelToViewport` regression test.\n\n## Smoke evidence\n\nEnd-to-end verified on this branch with a real `entire review` run:\n- ✅ Mouse wheel scrolls through buffered events\n- ✅ Long AssistantText events wrap to multiple readable lines (no `…` truncation mid-content)\n- Drill-in chrome and key delegation confirmed via unit tests (`TestDetailFrame_*`, `TestTUIModel_DelegatesScrollKeysToViewport`, `TestTUIModel_DelegatesMouseWheelToViewport`)\n\n## What this PR does NOT do (explicitly deferred)\n\n- **Agent-failure visibility** (the \"dashboard shows ✓ done but tally says 1 failed\" inconsistency): fixed by [#1167](https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1167) which is already open with reviews approved. Once #1167 lands, the synthetic RunError emission from `proc.Wait()` errors will surface in the drill-in event log AND the runFinishedMsg handler will propagate Failed status correctly. Independent of this PR.\n- **Env-handshake / session-tagging bug** (the \"review session was not tagged as a review\" warning when synthesis is declined): separate follow-up. The PR fix here doesn't claim to address that path.\n- **Per-agent progress streaming**: agents like claude-code `-p` and codex `exec` buffer their stdout until the response is complete, so during the run the drill-in shows mostly `[started]` until the buffer flushes at the end. Improving live streaming requires per-agent investigation (different output modes for each agent CLI) — that's its own brainstorm.\n- **Bubbletea v1 → v2 mouse API**: I originally planned `tea.WithMouseCellMotion()` as a Program option (v1 idiom); v2 moved this to `View.MouseMode`. Adapted accordingly with regression test.\n\n## Test plan\n\n- [x] `mise run fmt && mise run lint` — 0 issues\n- [x] `go test ./cmd/entire/cli/review/ -count=1` — all green (includes 3 new tests for wrap, viewport init, scroll-key delegation, mouse-wheel delegation, post-finish access, cancellation feedback)\n- [x] Manual smoke: mouse wheel scrolls during real multi-agent review\n- [x] Unit-tested all key delegation paths (keyboard + mouse)\n\n## Two-stage subagent review per task\n\nBoth Commits 1 and 2 went through spec-compliance + code-quality review:\n- **Commit 1 (viewport)**: spec ✅, code quality ✅\n- **Commit 2 (post-finish + cancellation)**: spec ✅, code quality ✅ (after `6fb988b43` doc fixup)\n- **Commit 3 (mouse mode)**: DONE_WITH_CONCERNS — accepted v2 API adaptation, then the missing routing was found and fixed in `c279308b2` with regression test\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n<!-- CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\n---\n\n> [!NOTE]\n> **Medium Risk**\n> Moderate risk: replaces manual drill-in scrolling with a `viewport.Model` and changes key/mouse handling and cancellation/exit semantics, which can affect interactive TUI behavior but is well-covered by new tests.\n> \n> **Overview**\n> Improves the Ctrl+O drill-in by switching its body rendering to a `bubbles/v2/viewport`, so long `AssistantText` now **wraps to multiple lines**, preserves embedded newlines as paragraph breaks, and supports standard pager keys plus mouse-wheel scrolling.\n> \n> Refactors the drill-in renderer into `detailFrame` (chrome + padding) and removes the prior manual scroll/windowing logic, adding helpers like `wrapDisplayWidth` and viewport-driven auto-tail that preserves user scroll when not at bottom.\n> \n> Updates run-finish and cancellation UX: post-finish no longer exits on any key (explicit `q/Esc/Enter/Ctrl+C` only, while `Ctrl+O` still works), and Ctrl+C now enters a visible *cancelling* state on first press with a second Ctrl+C force-quitting. Tests are updated/expanded to cover wrapping, viewport delegation, mouse routing, and the new exit/cancel behavior.\n> \n> <sup>Reviewed by [Cursor Bugbot](https://cursor.com/bugbot) for commit c279308b22d7bc77a43ad2f580523023d302b3c1. Configure [here](https://www.cursor.com/dashboard/bugbot).</sup>\n<!-- /CURSOR_SUMMARY -->","title":"feat(review): viewport-driven drill-in with wrap, scroll, and post-finish access","base":"main","base_sha":"40d00ad55459990a0cd6412b19d859c02498266c","head":"feat/review-detail-viewport","head_sha":"c279308b22d7bc77a43ad2f580523023d302b3c1","merge_commit_sha":"83ec38611832c7bcb1ada2d694cf51514384c7d6","user":{"login":"peyton-alt","name":"peyton-alt","email":null,"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/249787869?v=4","id":249787869},"requested_reviewers":null,"requested_team_reviewers":[{"slug":"cli-maintainers","name":"cli-maintainers"}],"diff":null,"comments":null,"