{"timestamp":"2026-05-12T02:23:27.302Z","type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"function_call_output","call_id":"call_eL1cUhYZ06kx3d00o1bwK95w","output":"Chunk ID: 7ccb02\nWall time: 0.4561 seconds\nProcess exited with code 0\nOriginal token count: 2342\nOutput:\n{\"data\":{\"repository\":{\"pullRequest\":{\"number\":1184,\"url\":\"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1184\",\"title\":\"feat(review): viewport-driven drill-in with wrap, scroll, and post-finish access\",\"state\":\"OPEN\",\"reviewThreads\":{\"nodes\":[{\"id\":\"PRRT_kwDOQyo98M6BRaBC\",\"isResolved\":false,\"isOutdated\":false,\"path\":\"cmd/entire/cli/review/tui_model.go\",\"line\":393,\"startLine\":391,\"originalLine\":393,\"originalStartLine\":391,\"resolvedBy\":null,\"comments\":{\"nodes\":[{\"id\":\"PRRC_kwDOQyo98M7AHv9c\",\"body\":\"The comment on isPostFinishExitKey is now inaccurate: Ctrl+C is handled in the early `if m.finished && !m.detailMode` block (it quits immediately) rather than being “handled separately in the normal switch” for double-press semantics. Please update the comment to match the actual control flow to avoid future confusion/regressions.\\n\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-05-12T02:03:14Z\",\"updatedAt\":\"2026-05-12T02:03:15Z\",\"author\":{\"login\":\"copilot-pull-request-reviewer\"}}]}},{\"id\":\"PRRT_kwDOQyo98M6BRaBT\",\"isResolved\":false,\"isOutdated\":false,\"path\":\"cmd/entire/cli/review/tui_model.go\",\"line\":195,\"startLine\":190,\"originalLine\":195,\"originalStartLine\":190,\"resolvedBy\":null,\"comments\":{\"nodes\":[{\"id\":\"PRRC_kwDOQyo98M7AHv94\",\"body\":\"This comment references an exact line number in an external dependency (`bubbles/v2/viewport.go:696`). That will become stale as soon as the dependency updates. Consider referencing the relevant type/method (e.g., “viewport handles tea.MouseWheelMsg”) without a hard-coded line number.\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-05-12T02:03:14Z\",\"updatedAt\":\"2026-05-12T02:03:15Z\",\"author\":{\"login\":\"copilot-pull-request-reviewer\"}}]}},{\"id\":\"PRRT_kwDOQyo98M6BRaBh\",\"isResolved\":false,\"isOutdated\":false,\"path\":\"cmd/entire/cli/review/tui_detail.go\",\"line\":59,\"startLine\":59,\"originalLine\":59,\"originalStartLine\":null,\"resolvedBy\":null,\"comments\":{\"nodes\":[{\"id\":\"PRRC_kwDOQyo98M7AHv-O\",\"body\":\"The buildEventLines doc comment says the result is suitable for feeding into a viewport via `SetContent`, but the model currently uses `viewport.Model.SetContentLines`. Consider updating the comment to match the actual API in use (or clarify both options) so future edits don’t drift.\\n\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-05-12T02:03:14Z\",\"updatedAt\":\"2026-05-12T02:03:15Z\",\"author\":{\"login\":\"copilot-pull-request-reviewer\"}}]}},{\"id\":\"PRRT_kwDOQyo98M6BRgba\",\"isResolved\":false,\"isOutdated\":false,\"path\":\"cmd/entire/cli/review/tui_model.go\",\"line\":402,\"startLine\":402,\"originalLine\":402,\"originalStartLine\":null,\"resolvedBy\":null,\"comments\":{\"nodes\":[{\"id\":\"PRRC_kwDOQyo98M7AH5Ef\",\"body\":\"### Missing `KeyEsc` alias in post-finish exit check\\n\\n**Low Severity**\\n\\n<!-- DESCRIPTION START -->\\n`isPostFinishExitKey` checks `tea.KeyEscape` but not `tea.KeyEsc`, while the main Escape handler on line 355 defensively checks both (`tea.KeyEscape || tea.KeyEsc`). If the two constants ever differ, an Esc press on the post-finish dashboard would skip the exit guard, fall into the main switch's Escape case (which is a no-op outside detail mode), and silently fail to quit.\\n<!-- DESCRIPTION END -->\\n\\n<!-- BUGBOT_BUG_ID: 19bfeb3c-eda5-4c51-8ccf-0d830dca7d9a -->\\n\\n<!-- LOCATIONS START\\ncmd/entire/cli/review/tui_model.go#L393-L402\\ncmd/entire/cli/review/tui_model.go#L354-L355\\nLOCATIONS END -->\\n<details>\\n<summary>Additional Locations (1)</summary>\\n\\n- [`cmd/entire/cli/review/tui_model.go#L354-L355`](https://github.com/entireio/cli/blob/c279308b22d7bc77a43ad2f580523023d302b3c1/cmd/entire/cli/review/tui_model.go#L354-L355)\\n\\n</details>\\n\